WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.610
Class 3-B?

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.760
Ms. Kuroi!

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.920
Yeah, yeah...

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.420
Morning, you two.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:33.670
Yo.

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:34.960
Good morning.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.210
You remembered to wear your winter uniform.

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:37.880
Come on...

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:39.040
It's not like I'm Tsukasa.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:39.760
What?!

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:42.010
But the hot weather isn't over yet...

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:44.470
They could let us wear our summer uniforms a little longer.

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:47.850
And when we have to wear
summer uniforms, it gets cold sometimes...

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.310
They should just let us choose.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.350
Right?

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.560
The switch is more to give students a change in pace.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.280
Else there would be more slackers like you two.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.780
This doesn't happen in our family...

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.240
...but I've heard that some parents monitor...

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.370
...their daughter's cell phones and e-mail.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:08.620
I've heard of that on occasion.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.290
Is it like that for you?

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.710
Probably not.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.170
Your dad's the type to smother...

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.630
...but I guess he wouldn't do anything you wouldn't like.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.090
That might be part of it...

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.640
My dad also uses the computer.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.310
Maybe it's 'cause he knows how  embarrassing it is when someone else looks at your D drive.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:29.180
D...

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:29.720
What?

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:33.730
We're had all these classes and stuff this summer...

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:34.480
In the end...

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.230
I only got to have fun with the fireworks and Ariake.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.400
So you still go to Comiket.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:39.900
Comiket?!

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.280
Well, you know...

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.200
As a result, my wallet's feeling pretty lonely.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.240
How much did you spend?

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.240
You never know when to draw the line.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.080
If you assume each book is a thousand yen...

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.580
Around forty to fifty thousand yen total?

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:53.660
Why you...

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.460
There's a limit to how clueless a
person can be about the value of money!

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.290
Still, Kagami...

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.460
There's this thing called market price.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:02.590
And it's pretty expensive to publish your own stuff.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.050
That's not what I meant!

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.430
I'm talking about how you don't
feel anything after spending so much!

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.760
It may be September...

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.640
...but it's still hot.

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.270
That's right.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.850
It seems especially hot this year.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:17.440
And there's talk about global warming.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.270
Yu-chan can't put up with too much heat...

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:24.490
...so she's been resting in an
air-conditioned room most of the time.

00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:27.070
That's what Tsukasa's been doing the whole time.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:27.910
But she's just lazy.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:29.700
Well...

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.910
Dad and I join in...

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.210
...and we all lie around looking like a 小 character.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.290
小?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.290
Shouldn't it be 川?

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:39.090
Nah.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.630
Dad's always in the middle.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.630
Your family never changes.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.680
And I guess Yutaka-chan's gotten used to it.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:51.220
Hey, hey!

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.930
Doing good, Yutaka?

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.640
I'm here to play!

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:56.560
Sis!

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.100
Oh?

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.560
Who's this?

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.310
My friend...

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.400
Minami Iwasaki-chan.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.060
So this is the Minami-chan Yutaka's always talking about.

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.410
S-Sis!

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.200
<i>So she has a reason for hope right next to her...</i>

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.870
<i>I'm a little jealous.</i>

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:15.830
Man...

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:17.830
I'd heard all the fuss...

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:20.250
...but you sure are pretty.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.260
You wowed me!

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.210
Want something to drink?

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.670
Beer then!

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:26.550
Huh?!

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:28.090
Didn't you drive here?!

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.470
Just kiddin'!

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.640
Barley tea's fine!

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.970
<i>I see.</i>

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.850
<i>One absorbs from the other...</i>

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:36.060
<i>Absorption, is it...</i>

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:49.820
Oh...

00:04:49.820 --> 00:04:51.120
It's the Yassai Mossai?

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.910
I always get sleepy at night.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.870
Do you have any good ideas?

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:57.330
Instead of forcing yourself to stay up...

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.830
...why don't you wake up early and work on it?

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.000
You'll probably feel better.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:01.920
I see!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.040
You're right!

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.550
I'll wake up early and work hard.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:12.510
<i>Huh?</i>

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:15.470
<i>Why is it the same time I always get up?</i>

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:16.310
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:18.600
<i>I vaguely remember turning
something off at some point...</i>

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:21.480
Even when I wake up early...

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.690
...I just roll over and go back to sleep.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:25.110
You have no willpower...

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.650
Maybe I should just try harder...

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:29.070
...and work on it at night.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:31.490
I doubt rubbing your eyes while nodding off...

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:34.200
...will improve the results.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.120
Why don't you have someone wake you up?

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.000
Mom and the others wake up early.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:39.890
Right, Mom?

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:41.460
Yes, yes.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:42.920
I'll wake you up.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:45.670
This can't fail.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.460
Sis is amazing.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.430
Mom!

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.800
I told you to wake me up!

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.850
I did.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:56.430
You even answered me back.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:58.640
I don't know anything about that.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:00.360
You don't remember?

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:06.610
Big Sister forgot her lunch...

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:18.370
Thanks!

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:24.330
It feels kind of weird to walk
through the hallway of a different grade.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:27.000
You can feel a little pressure...

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.800
I know what you mean.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:32.260
<i>Yu-chan probably drew everybody's attention.</i>

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:33.380
<i>Being the way she is...</i>

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:36.970
Usually, it's just your imagination...

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:39.470
...but when you walk through a
hallway for upperclassmen or underclassmen...

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:42.810
...you get this feeling that everybody's looking at you, right?

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:45.520
I already tend to stand out 'cause I'm smaller...

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.400
...but when it's because they're
upperclassmen, the pressure is more intense.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:53.150
I enjoy receiving that kind of attention.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:54.660
Really...

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:58.870
But I don't attract much attention when I'm in the first-year's area.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:01.250
They don't realize I'm an upperclassman.

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:04.210
Patty-chan.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:04.750
Hi!

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:05.420
Hello there.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:07.500
Are you heading to work?

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:08.380
That's right.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:10.920
I signed up for too many shifts this week.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.470
Aren't you still working?

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:14.470
That's right.

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:16.930
We're pretty popular.

00:07:16.930 --> 00:07:19.180
The A-boys are all over us.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.020
A-boys?

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:25.440
It's what you call boys who look like they totally belong in Akiba.

00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:29.520
But Narimiya-kun was a little different.

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.110
You're getting accustomed to Japan.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.940
A little too accustomed, don't you think?

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:39.910
I just had a great idea!

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:44.590
I'll write it down once I'm done with my bath.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:51.840
H-Huh?

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:52.920
I can't remember...

00:07:52.920 --> 00:07:55.220
This is what happens when I don't jot it down immediately...

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:56.260
And it was funny...

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:57.930
Hilarious, even!

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:02.220
Another exhausting day...

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:09.190
<i>That might be a funny idea.</i>

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:12.340
<i>I'll write it down when I wake up tomorrow.</i>

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.150
Er...

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:17.860
That's weird...

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.120
What was it again?

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.280
I'm positive it was a good idea.

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:24.410
Should have just gotten out of bed and written it down.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.130
Man!

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:37.220
I even got out of bed this time!

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:39.300
Why do you forget dreams so quickly?

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.970
I'm positive that it was hilarious!

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.520
So...

00:08:48.520 --> 00:08:50.980
Make sure you all talk it over within your group.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:53.440
Since we're going all the way to Kyoto and Nara...

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.440
...you better check up on all the hot tourist spots.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:59.410
Aren't we going through all the hot spots by bus?

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.080
Those will just be the typical places...

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:04.330
...so they won't be that fun.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:05.330
Well now...

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:06.870
That's a blunt way to put it...

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.800
So Iris came in here...

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.680
I will now guide you through the former capital of Nara.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:26.810
Almost 1,300 years have passed since it became the capital in 710.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:27.600
While in Nara...

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:32.060
...I hope you enjoy my historical Nara narration.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:36.320
Nara!

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:36.980
Nara narration!

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:38.530
Were we supposed to laugh?

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:44.070
Sorry for the wait!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.290
This is the main body...

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:51.330
So the little things around it are options!

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.000
You're gonna get hit by lightning.

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:13.980
No!

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:22.610
I'm all sticky...

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:23.780
And stinky...

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:25.320
I'm all stinky now!

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:25.870
Here, here, here.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:26.700
Indeed.

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:27.990
What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:30.410
Please, please.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:34.420
They probably want you to take their picture.

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:37.460
Um... Um...

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:39.340
Click. Click.

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:40.340
Okay?

00:10:40.340 --> 00:10:42.880
This is when you can tell how much somebody's been studying.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:43.880
Like you're one to talk.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:45.390
Um...

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:46.680
Sis.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.100
How do you say "cheese" in Indian?

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:51.350
You mean Hindi, right?

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.560
Um...

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.020
Uh...

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:57.900
Genius girl Kagami can't do any better.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.110
Um...

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:01.780
I believe that Indians will understand English.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:02.950
That's right!

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:05.110
"Say cheese!" should be fine, yeah?

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:06.320
Okay.

00:11:06.320 --> 00:11:08.280
Say cheese!

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:09.490
You know how...

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:12.960
...couples pop out of nowhere during school trips?

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:15.860
Can't miss the school trip event.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:17.840
Perhaps...

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:19.960
...being away from school...

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.590
...gives people a sense of freedom?

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.300
Kinda like a now or never thing.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:27.850
I'm embarrassed to say that...

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:30.760
...I'm unable to sleep with a different pillow.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.560
I'm embarrassed to say that...

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:35.640
...I can't sleep peacefully without this nearby.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:37.560
I'm embarrassed to say that...

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:41.440
...I can't sleep if I haven't turned
this on at least once during the day.

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.030
Everyone.

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:47.200
The bus will soon pass Kiyomizu Temple.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.700
The hill leading to Kiyomizu Temple...

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.330
...is known as Three-year Hill.

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:52.410
Legend says that...

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.910
...if you trip and fall here, you'll die in three years.

00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:56.080
Three-year Hill will become...

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:57.830
...your Boo-hoo Hill.

00:11:58.490 --> 00:12:00.210
Does it count if you break down laughing?

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:01.590
Okay?

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:04.010
We'll be moving around in individual groups now.

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:06.050
Keep an eye out for traffic.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:09.010
We'll regroup at 12:30 in front of Chion-in.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.550
Don't be late.

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:13.680
Anybody who's late gets to write a
happy 20-page report when we get back.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:15.850
Sure about that?

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:18.520
Let's give it a try.

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:25.650
The Dragon Slayer's probably about this heavy.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:30.160
We're really high up.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:33.370
You know how the saying goes,
"Like you're going to jump off Kiyomizu..."

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:36.330
...but if you really jumped, wouldn't you die?

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:38.620
Does it mean that you no longer care what happens?

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.880
You're so pragmatic, Kagami.

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:42.130
Look, look!

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:43.380
It says marriage.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:46.630
This place seems to be famous for its god of marriage.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.590
They really spell it out for you.

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:49.840
Look.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:51.680
You can draw love fortunes.

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:53.140
Let's all give it a try.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:55.100
Let's do it!

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:01.440
Guess I can't tell these apart...

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.110
Isn't that obvious?

00:13:04.770 --> 00:13:05.400
This one!

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:08.360
Great fortune!

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:10.950
Lucky you, Kona-chan.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:11.660
My.

00:13:11.660 --> 00:13:13.120
I drew good fortune.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.830
That's fine.

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.370
Now what did I get...

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:19.040
Half fortune?

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:20.010
What's this?

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:22.500
I-I guess you only get half a fortune.

00:13:22.500 --> 00:13:24.840
Which means it's half bad.

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:27.340
Not like I care about love fortunes.

00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:30.220
So cute!

00:13:31.090 --> 00:13:32.090
That looks nice.

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:32.680
Nah.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:34.180
Kagami would want this.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.770
What's that supposed to mean?

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.520
I'll get one of these.

00:13:40.180 --> 00:13:41.020
Kagami! Kagami!

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:42.230
You forgot this!

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:43.230
I'm not buying it!

00:13:43.230 --> 00:13:43.980
Then what about this?

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:44.650
No!

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:47.610
You should be careful.

00:13:52.270 --> 00:13:53.940
Marriage Wishes
Marriage Wishes

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:56.160
This one says, "Konata is my waifu."

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:56.660
Marriage Wishes
Marriage Wishes

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:57.910
Okay.

00:13:57.910 --> 00:13:59.540
Everyone's here, right?

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.500
We'll have lunch after we've gone in the hotel.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.900
Let's get going.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.590
Take us there please.

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:10.880
They said that Koizumi's character
song was written in an IZAM style.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:12.470
Teacher!

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:14.470
Someone's chasing us from behind!

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:15.470
What?!

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:22.390
This is like the Hokkaido shoot all over again!

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:22.760
Don't ditch me!

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:24.770
You have to go, "***tel!"

00:14:24.770 --> 00:14:25.770
That idiot.

00:14:25.770 --> 00:14:27.650
He's getting assigned a 50-page report!

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:28.440
Driver!

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.280
Sorry, could you stop for a second?

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:34.040
See you later.

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.390
Doesn't even hurt!

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:58.930
The Golden Pavilion Temple is golden...

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:01.020
...but the Silver Pavilion Temple isn't silver, huh?

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.840
They wanted to group it with the Golden Pavilion Temple...

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:04.060
Click.

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:06.310
...so they named it silver to go along with golden.

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:07.310
Click.

00:15:07.310 --> 00:15:07.890
It was never silver to begin with.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:08.610
Click.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:09.690
It was never silver to begin with.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:11.110
I wonder if it's like Poke***...

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:13.820
With Sapphire and Ruby and stuff.

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:16.490
No comment?

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:19.830
Our family's shrine was on the news.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:22.620
We only have one day left.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:25.330
Our plan for free time is all set.

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:28.670
Tomorrow is the beginning of our true school trip!

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:30.630
Off we go to the holy land!

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:31.590
Right...

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:53.740
D-Does this count as being in front of the hotel?

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.200
Did you wait long?

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:58.800
So...

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.660
What did you want to talk about?

00:16:03.490 --> 00:16:06.120
You're the only person I can talk to about this.

00:16:18.670 --> 00:16:20.390
Please give me that doll!

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:22.810
Doll?

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:23.060
You know...

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:26.770
The one you bought from the Kiyomizu Temple souvenir shop!

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.650
The Yatsuhashi character.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.060
Ya-Yatsuhashi-kun?

00:16:31.060 --> 00:16:31.440
Yeah!

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:32.230
That one!

00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:34.990
I really liked it and wanted one.

00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:37.110
But if someone saw me buying one...

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:38.950
...they'd probably all make fun of me!

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:39.950
I'm begging you!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:43.080
Thank you!

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:44.490
I'm eternally in your debt!

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.750
Don't tell anybody about this!

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.420
Yes, yes.

00:16:57.420 --> 00:17:00.470
I'm reading this book about four brothers.

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:01.340
****** of the Dragon Kings?

00:17:01.340 --> 00:17:01.600
I can't take it off!

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:02.010
That's right.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:02.680
Come to think of it...

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:02.920
The steam within cooled off...

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:04.680
That could make a pretty good anime.

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:05.600
...and formed a vacuum.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:06.810
They did an anime adaptation a while back.

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.890
If you press on the sides a little...

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:08.940
...that should allow air to enter and make the lid easier to remove.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.270
Really?

00:17:10.270 --> 00:17:11.650
I had no idea!

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.640
I think they went up to the
fourth volume of the original.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:14.900
In that case...

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:16.360
But those books are...

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.530
I'm sorry!

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:18.900
So sorry!

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:20.910
Putting on a show till the very end.

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.210
I've already looked up the directions.

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:32.790
Is it really okay for us to visit?

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:35.710
We'll just be looking from the outside so it's okay.

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:39.390
There's no need to go that far just 'cause we're in Kyoto.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:40.550
Tsk. Tsk. Tsk.

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.930
You don't understand the geek's idea of romance.

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:45.510
I don't want to.

00:17:50.180 --> 00:17:51.980
Not much here.

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.940
It makes it easier to concentrate on their job so this works.

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:03.030
It's a pretty ordinary-looking building.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:06.290
They limit their workload so this works.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.000
Was it really necessary to buy these in Kyoto?

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:16.420
That's embarrassing!

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:17.380
Who cares?

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:19.210
It's a little something for remembering this day!

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.050
Sis!

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:20.840
Let's take a picture together!

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:22.470
It's for commemorating this trip.

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:26.970
Since we came all the way to Kyoto.

00:18:26.970 --> 00:18:28.930
What does this have to do with Kyoto?

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:37.400
Tsukasa and I made it back in one piece.

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:39.650
Tsukasa's already asleep though.

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:43.110
I figured you'd be sulking in bed.

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:45.570
Why would I be doing that?

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:48.080
Did you put up the sticker photo?

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:50.450
How could I put up something so embarrassing?

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:57.090
Something so embarrassing....

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:06.140
The school trip was this week...

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:08.220
I sure worked hard.

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:10.390
Okay.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:13.440
Time to spend the weekend gaming online for once.

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:24.780
Good lucky!

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:28.240
Here's another crazy episode of Lucky Channel!

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:29.790
I'm your navigator, Akira Kogami!

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:31.790
I'm the assistant...

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.290
Daisuke Ono.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:35.790
Lucky Channel is already on the twenty-first episode!

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:36.880
That's right.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.630
We're finally getting close to the end.

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:39.290
Well, then...

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:41.300
Let's get straight to this corner...

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:43.050
This week's...

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:44.300
Bend!

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:49.180
Who is it?

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:50.700
What?

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:52.310
I brought your water.

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:04.490
What is this?!

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:05.700
It's warm!

00:20:05.700 --> 00:20:07.410
How am I supposed to drink this?!

00:20:07.860 --> 00:20:10.410
I'd rather have something out of a vending machine.

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:16.210
Don't mess with me!

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:17.580
You...

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:18.670
Why, you...

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.920
What do you think I've had to put up with this whole time?!

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:23.630
All your damn selfish requests one after the next!

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:24.880
Mi-Minoru?

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:27.090
Well, I'm gonna speak my mind today!

00:20:27.090 --> 00:20:30.220
Do you know how I felt when I was doing this corner?!

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:32.220
I'd have to work at CoCo**** every day!

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:34.850
That's better pay than my voice acting work!

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:37.190
Thanks to you, I'm working full-time now!

00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:38.770
Before I come kiss your ass here...

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:39.940
...I'm over there frying cutlets!

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.980
Which means you're more suited for that work.

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:46.320
And what the hell?!

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:48.110
Why are you sitting there, Ono boy?!

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.610
That's my seat!

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:51.990
You were abandoned.

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.620
By the director and the producer.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.000
What's that?!

00:20:55.740 --> 00:20:57.960
They acted too quickly!

00:20:57.960 --> 00:20:59.540
I'm a late bloomer!

00:20:59.540 --> 00:21:01.840
I can go from here to Starga**r in no time!

00:21:02.040 --> 00:21:03.670
You can?

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:04.670
Weally?

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:08.010
Sittin' there making fun of me...

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:09.680
Screw working with Hine**su...

00:21:09.680 --> 00:21:11.930
Or Lo** and Be***...

00:21:12.800 --> 00:21:14.810
I quit.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:18.480
I quit this stupid show, damn it!

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:20.850
Take that!

00:21:20.850 --> 00:21:22.100
Who gives a damn about Lucky Channel?!

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:22.980
Shiraishi Minoru-san!

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:24.900
What are you doing, morons?!

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:29.450
What are you filming there?!

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:31.870
What's with the Cape of Thirty Years?!

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:33.200
If you wanna play with that...

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:36.240
...I'm gonna be thirty soon!

00:21:36.240 --> 00:21:38.870
I'm talking about you....

00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:13.620
Well, next time on Lucky Star:

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.160
I'm Akira Kogami!

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:17.120
I'm Daisuke Ono.

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:28.470
Okay.

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:29.590
That's it for the animal talk.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.970
That was in animal, huh?

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:32.590
Next time:

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:34.260
There Over Here.

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:36.140
I can cross the goal line now, can't I?

00:23:37.760 --> 00:23:38.680
Ramen set!
